Description: Monthly E. coli monitoring of drinking water along the chain from
    borehole sources to household storage in four Ugandan districts (Nakaseke,
    Kaabong, Kumi and Luuka) between November 2024 and September 2025. For each
    borehole, water was sampled at the source and, in three households using
    it, from the container used to carry water home and from the drinking
    water storage container. Samples were analysed by membrane filtration and
    classified into five contamination levels. The package provides four tidy
    datasets: field visits to boreholes, field visits to households, water
    samples with their laboratory results, and laboratory blanks.
